{
  "_doc": "Achievement catalog. One track of permanent, claim once goals, read by lib/achievement-engine.js. Every achievement has a `track` (board section: combat, adventure, collection, wealth, social, mastery), a `tier` (see `tiers`), a `check`, and a `reward`. A check is EITHER { metric, goal } (progress from player.quests.lifetime, the shared counter store fed by recordQuestEvent) OR { stat, goal } (progress snapshotted live from the player record by achievement-engine's STATS evaluators). Stat progress is stamped sticky on first observation: once an achievement counts as unlocked it stays unlocked even if the stat later drops (you spend your hoard, the hoard achievement stays yours). Rewards use the quest reward vocabulary (see quests.json): solars|xp|gems|stamina|seasonPoints as a plain amount, or item|character through addOwnedSeasonContent. Copy is player-facing: no dashes, commas and colons only.",
